    "long_instructions": "**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Use your pipeline’s `predict` method to generate predictions for all of the test inputs.\r\n2. Score how well your model performed. If your model is a classification model, use `accuracy_score` to score what percentage of predictions your model got correct. If your model is a regression model, use `mean_absolute_error` to score the average error in your model’s predictions.\r\n3. Print your model’s performance.\r\n4. To improve your model’s performance, you can try different hyperparameters for your neural network. Try experimenting with `hidden_layer_sizes` and `max_iter`.\r\n5. If you have time, consider adding other performance metrics too (for example, performance for certain kinds of inputs).\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nYou can import `accuracy_score` or `mean_absolute_error` from `sklearn.metrics`. Then, call the score function by providing the actual outputs and the predicted outputs.\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\r\nfrom sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error\r\n```\r\n\r\nGive your `MLPClassifier` or `MLPRegressor` arguments like `hidden_layer_sizes=(M,), max_iter=N` to experiment with different iterations and hidden layer sizes.\r\n\r\nAsk AI Tutor for help if you get stuck!\r\n",
